{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-437761-r4518279","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Sabich (Vegetable and Pita Sandwich)","sourcePageId":437761,"sourceRevision":"4518279","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:19:57Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Sabich%20(Vegetable%20and%20Pita%20Sandwich)&oldid=4518279","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T14:15:46.048Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Israeli recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Middle Eastern recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sandwiches","Category:Recipes using bread","Category:Recipes using cucumber","Category:Recipes using eggplant","Category:Recipes using hard-cooked egg","Category:Recipes using hummus","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"15ff0c30e372a3e85f4b7f236f32d527d240c1153f8c3785533fed4a1ddfe7d5","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sandwich recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Sandwiches|Sandwiches]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Israel|Cuisine of Israel]]\n\n'''Sabich''' is a popular Israeli [[Cookbook:Sandwiches|sandwich]] based on what Iraqi Jews ate on Sabbath morning, featuring fried [[Cookbook:Eggplant|eggplant]], boiled [[Cookbook:Potatoes|potato]], and hard-boiled [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]. Instead of serving the ingredients on a tray, as was traditional, sabich stuffs everything in a pita.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Israeli salad ===\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], cored and [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. [[Cookbook:Cucumber|cucumber]], chopped\n*1 [[Cookbook:Onions|onion]], chopped\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n\n=== Sandwich ===\n*1 [[Cookbook:Eggplant|eggplant]], sliced into 1 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]] rounds\n*4 [[Cookbook:Hard Boiled Eggs|hard-boiled eggs]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n*[[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]], for frying\n*4 [[Cookbook:Pita|pita breads]]\n*¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Hummus|hummus]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Tahini|tahini]]\n*Amba sauce\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Israeli salad ===\n#Put the tomatoes, cucumber, onion, and parsley in a bowl.\n#Take another small bowl and mix the lemon juice, oil, and salt.\n#Pour the dressing over the vegetables and toss well, leave it to stand for a couple of minutes.\n\n=== Sandwich ===\n#Meanwhile, heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high temperature. When the oil has become hot enough, [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] the eggplant slices until they turn golden brown. Place the golden eggplant slices on a paper towel to remove the excess oil.\n#Spread the hummus evenly in each pita bread\n#Stuff the pitas with the slices of fried eggplants and the boiled eggs.\n#Spoon over some of the Israeli salad, drizzle the tahini and amba over the pitas, and serve.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* Amba is pickled mango that is very popular in the Middle east. It may be difficult to find amba in some stores, but you can use hot sauce instead.\n\n[[Category:Israeli recipes]]\n[[Category:Middle Eastern recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sandwiches]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hard-cooked egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using eggplant]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hummus]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Sabich (Vegetable and Pita Sandwich)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 tomatoes, cored and chopped","sourceText":"2 tomatoes, cored and chopped","amountText":"2 tomatoes, cored and chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ ea. cucumber, chopped","sourceText":"½ ea. cucumber, chopped","amountText":"½ ea. cucumber, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 onion, chopped","amountText":"1 onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tbsp minced parsley","sourceText":"1 tbsp minced parsley","amountText":"1 tbsp minced parsley","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tbsp lemon juice","sourceText":"2 tbsp lemon juice","amountText":"2 tbsp lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"2 tbsp oil","sourceText":"2 tbsp oil","amountText":"2 tbsp oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 eggplant, sliced into 1 cm rounds","sourceText":"1 eggplant, sliced into 1 cm rounds","amountText":"1 eggplant, sliced into 1 cm rounds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"4 hard-boiled eggs, peeled and sliced","sourc